  "raw": {
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Professional-Counseling_R-097800-2": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Professional Counseling Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Education & Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria seeks three to four full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professors of Professional Counseling with an anticipated start date of January 2027. The position is located at the Victoria Campus. Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks three to four full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professors of Professional Counseling, with an anticipated start date of January 2027. The position is located at the Victoria Campus, and the successful candidate will maintain a regular presence on campus. Qualifications: The College of Education and Health Professions at Texas A&M University–Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position in Professional Counseling. The Master of Science in Professional Counseling program offers two CACREP-accredited concentrations: Clinical Mental Health Counseling and Professional School Counseling. We seek an individual with an earned doctorate in Counselor Education or a closely related field, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Candidates with a confirmed doctoral completion date will be considered. Candidates should identify with the counseling profession through active involvement in appropriate professional organizations and demonstrate experience in university teaching and clinical supervision of counselors-in-training. Candidates should demonstrate knowledge of CACREP standards, professional counseling practice, and the preparation of clinical mental health and/or professional school counselors. Candidates must be eligible for appropriate professional licensure or certification in the State of Texas. Successful candidates will: Teach master's-level courses in the CACREP core and courses supporting the Clinical Mental Health Counseling and Professional School Counseling concentrations in traditional and online formats (4-course or equivalent teaching load in the fall and spring semesters); Provide clinical supervision to counselors-in-training, including supervision of practicum and internship experiences and clinical site visits as appropriate; Advise and mentor graduate students throughout their academic and professional preparation; Participate in student recruitment, admissions, orientation, retention, and other program activities; Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement; Collaborate with public schools, school districts, clinical mental health agencies, healthcare organizations, and other community partners; Maintain active involvement in appropriate professional counseling organizations; Maintain an appropriate scholarly agenda consistent with expectations for a tenure-track faculty appointment; Encourage and mentor student participation in research and professional activities; and Contribute to the College and University's mission through assigned service. These responsibilities preserve the substantive expectations in the current ad, including teaching, curriculum development, clinical supervision, student mentoring and recruitment, community partnerships, professional involvement, scholarship, and accreditation work. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated excellence in graduate teaching in traditional and online environments, clinical supervision experience, and a strong commitment to counselor preparation. Additional preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Graduation from a CACREP-accredited doctoral program in Counselor Education and Supervision; Current or previous professional counseling licensure and/or Certified School Counselor (CSC) credentials; Eligibility for professional licensure or certification in Texas; Experience teaching CACREP-aligned graduate counseling coursework; Experience supervising counseling practicum and internship students; Experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and/or Professional School Counseling; Working knowledge of current CACREP standards and accreditation processes; Experience with program assessment, evaluation, and continuous improvement; Evidence of scholarly activity related to counseling, counselor education, clinical mental health counseling, school counseling, or counselor preparation; Experience teaching effectively in online and other technology-supported learning environments; Strong interpersonal, collaborative, and leadership skills; and A commitment to developing collaborative relationships with schools, counseling agencies, healthcare providers, and community partners. Appointment at the Associate Professor Rank: Appointment at the Associate Professor rank requires a record of excellence in university teaching and a record of scholarly research and publication commensurate with the candidate's experience and the University's expectations for appointment at that rank. Values: Texas A&M–Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin Oct 24, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit TAMUV Jobs . If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Chang Lee (leeC3@tamuv.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Instructor-or-Assistant-Professor-of-English--Fiction--Creative-Writing-_R-097533": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of English (Fiction, Creative Writing)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructor or Assistant Professor of English (Fiction, Creative Writing) Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A & M-Victoria seeks one full-time, non-tenure Instructor (with MFA) or one full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (with doctoral degree) of English (Fiction, Creative Writing) with a start date of August 2027. Qualifications : The Department of Humanities at Texas A & M-Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position in English. Qualified applicants must have a doctoral degree (Assistant Professor) or MFA (Instructor) by August 15, 2027 in English, creative writing, or a related field; demonstrate excellence in teaching; provide evidence of scholarly, creative, and professional activities; and be willing to teach service courses offered by the English faculty as needed, including composition and professional writing. Other classes would be assigned in accordance with department needs and the new hire’s teaching interests. As preferred qualifications, we seek a candidate specializing in fiction. Additional experience in creative nonfiction, genre fiction, publishing, and/or professional editing is welcome. Experience mentoring undergraduate writers and supporting first-generation students is especially welcomed. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in a small but vigorous English program, including fiction workshops, composition, and other courses aligned with program needs and the candidate’s expertise. Depending on program needs and qualifications, the candidate may also have opportunities to teach literature courses and/or contribute to the MFA program. The candidate will hold regular office hours on campus; provide student-centered instruction and support for undergraduate writers; participate in course and program development; maintain an active agenda of scholarly, creative, and/or professional activity; perform appropriate college and professional service; and work cooperatively with students, faculty, and staff. The candidate will also be required to maintain a consistent campus presence. This is a nine-month appointment. The annual teaching load is 24 credit hours (4/4) for an Assistant Professor appointment or 30 credit hours (5/5) for an Instructor appointment, depending on the candidate’s qualifications. The successful candidate will begin employment in Fall 2027. Values : Texas A & M-Victoria Values: Together We Rise · W isdom · E xcellence · R espect · I ntegrity · S tudents · E mpathy Setting : Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin October 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here . If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Raymond Stricklin (StricklinR@TAMUV.edu) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Associate-Professor---Psychology--Counseling-_R-097554-1": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor - Psychology (Counseling)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate/Assistant Professor - Psychology (Counseling) Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M-Victoria seeks two full-time, tenure-track instructors of Clinical or Counseling Psychology at the Assistant Professor and/or Associate Professor levels, with a start date of August 2027. Qualifications : The Department of Social Science at Texas A&M-Victoria invites applications for tenure-track positions in Clinical or Counseling Psychology. A doctoral degree in Psychology from an APA or CPA accredited clinical or counseling program is required. Candidates with a confirmed doctoral completion date will be considered. The applicant must be license-eligible in Texas. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate education and will contribute to a vibrant department that supports multiple majors, including Psychology, History, Political Science, and Criminal Justice. Applicants whose research is in any area of Clinical or Counseling Psychology are encouraged to apply. The Department of Social Science welcomes especially any applicant who examines the interplay of biological processes with psychological, social, and/or behavioral factors. Evidence of an active research agenda and the ability to publish in the field of expertise are expected. Teaching responsibilities may include in-person introductory and elective undergraduate courses in Psychology, as well as graduate courses in an in-person and blended online format (with synchronous and asynchronous elements) at the master’s level. The role may also require supervising students in their practical experiences, advising, and mentoring students to help them achieve their potential, and serving on university committees as needed. Responsibilities : The applicant will teach twelve credit hours per semester of both undergraduate and graduate Psychology courses, in-person and online, depending on the expertise of the applicant and departmental needs. The successful applicant is expected to direct student learning opportunities that might include undergraduate and graduate research, or other applied student experiences, and to contribute to the distinctive general education curriculum and the broader academic life on campus. Other expectations include research and scholarly activity, career advising, fostering connections with community organizations, maintaining a strong campus presence, and supporting student recruitment and retention efforts. Texas A&M–Victoria Values: Together We Rise · Wisdom · Excellence · Respect · Integrity · Students · Empathy Setting : Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP, and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M–Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball, and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here .   Application:  Review of applications will begin October 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here.   If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Andrew Baerg (BaergA@TAMUV.edu) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Kinesiology---Physical-Education_R-097416": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Education & Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria seeks two full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology, with an anticipated start date of January 2027. The position is located at the Victoria Campus. Qualifications: The College of Education and Health Professions at Texas A&M University-Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position in Kinesiology. We seek an individual with an earned doctorate in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Human Performance, Sports Management, Physical Education or a closely related field by December 2026. An ABD candidate may be considered, provided there is a clearly established completion date. Candidates should have evidence of strong teaching, research, and service and demonstrate an understanding of contemporary approaches to areas in kinesiology such as exercise physiology, physical activity, health and wellness, and/or human performance. Successful candidates will: · Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Kinesiology in traditional and online formats (4-course or equivalent teaching load in the fall and spring semesters); · Teach courses appropriate to the candidate's expertise in areas such as, motor development and learning, adapted physical activity, fitness and wellness, exercise science, human performance, or related areas; · Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement; · Maintain an appropriate scholarly agenda consistent with expectations for a tenure-track faculty appointment; and · Contribute to the college and university's mission through assigned service. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated excellence in university teaching in traditional and online environments and experience preparing future physical education teachers. Additional preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: · Experience in adapted physical education or adapted physical activity; · Knowledge of contemporary approaches to physical literacy, fitness education, motor skill development, and lifelong physical activity; · Professional credentials or experience related to fitness, strength and conditioning, coaching, or health and wellness; and · A commitment to developing collaborative relationships with schools, community organizations, and other regional partners. Values: Texas A & M-Victoria Values: Together We Rise · W isdom · E xcellence · R espect · I ntegrity · S tudents · E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here. Application: Review of applications will begin Oct. 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit TAMUV Jobs. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Chang Lee (leec3@tamuv.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Curriculum-and-Instruction---K-12-Mathematics-Specialist_R-097400": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Curriculum and Instruction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Curriculum and Instruction Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Education & Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria seeks up to six full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Curriculum and Instruction, with an anticipated start date of January 2027. The position is located at the Victoria Campus. Qualifications: The Department of Teacher Education at Texas A&M University-Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Curriculum and Instruction. We welcome applicants with expertise in the following areas of specialization: · K-12 Mathematics Education (2 positions) · K-12 Science Education (1 position) · Literacy Studies (2 positions) We seek an individual with an earned doctorate in Curriculum and Instruction or a closely related field with at least 18 graduate credit hours in one of the identified areas of specialization completed by December 2026. An ABD candidate may be considered, provided there is a clearly established completion date. They should also have evidence of strong teaching at the higher education level, and a minimum of three years of PK-12 classroom teaching experience in the content area. The successful candidate should possess a strong understanding of effective pedagogy across grade levels and a working knowledge of expectations for educator preparation and teacher certification. Successful candidates will: · Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in Curriculum and Instruction and in both traditional and online formats in content area (4-course or equivalent teaching load in the fall and spring semesters); · Teach and support methods courses serving candidates seeking EC-6, 4-8, and secondary content area certification, as appropriate; · Support undergraduate teacher preparation and graduate programs in Curriculum and Instruction; · Work collaboratively with faculty to strengthen candidates' content knowledge, pedagogical content knowledge, and effective use of evidence-based instructional practices; · Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement; · Maintain an appropriate scholarly agenda consistent with expectations for a tenure-track faculty appointment; and · Contribute to the department, college, and university's mission through assigned service. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated excellence in university teaching in traditional and online environments and experience preparing teachers to provide effective instruction in diverse PK–12 settings. Additional preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: · Knowledge of the Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills (TEKS) for content area, knowledge of Texas Education Agency (TEA), and Texas educator certification standards; · Experience with content area curriculum development, assessment, and data-informed instruction; · Experience working with preservice and/or practicing teachers; · Experience supporting teacher candidates preparing for Texas content area certification examinations; · An understanding of the structures and needs of PK-12 schools and school systems; and · A commitment to developing collaborative relationships with schools, districts, Education Service Centers, and other educational partners. Values: Texas A & M-Victoria Values: Together We Rise · W isdom · E xcellence · R espect · I ntegrity · S tudents · E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here. Application: Review of applications will begin Oct. 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit TAMUV Jobs. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact Mary Lasater (LasaterM@TAMUV.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Assistant-Professor---Chemistry_R-097520-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor - Chemistry Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Natural & Applied Science Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria seeks one full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Chemistry with a start date of August 2027. Qualifications: The Department of Natural Sciences and Mathematics at Texas A&M University-Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position in Chemistry. We are seeking a chemist with a Ph.D. in inorganic, organic, or related areas of chemistry. Candidates with a confirmed Ph.D. completion date will be considered. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate education and will contribute to a vibrant department that supports Biology majors and pre-health students. Teaching responsibilities include general inorganic and organic chemistry lectures and associated laboratories. The area of research specialization is open. Evidence of an active research agenda and the ability to publish in the field of expertise is expected. Responsibilities: The applicant will teach twelve credit hours per semester of General Inorganic and Organic Chemistry courses and associated laboratories. The successful applicant to this position is expected to direct student learning opportunities that might include undergraduate research or other applied student experiences and to contribute to the distinctive general education curriculum and the broader academic life on campus. Other expectations include research and scholarly activity, career advising, fostering connections with community organizations, maintaining a strong campus presence, and supporting student recruitment and retention efforts. Texas A & M-Victoria Values: Together We Rise · W isdom · E xcellence · R espect · I ntegrity · S tudents · E mpathy Setting : Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here. Application: Review of applications will begin October 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here . If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Jang Woo Park (ParkJ1@TAMUV.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
